{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/969649-alternate-themes-and-motivations","id":969649,"title":"Alternate themes and motivations","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-14T21:44:28-07:00","id":969649,"title":"Alternate themes and motivations","content":"I was wondering, what are some themes/motivations/justifications you've come up with and used, other than the &quot;teaching lessons&quot; theme? Because I think it can be done well, but I understand that a lot of people don't like it, and there's a lot more potential than just being J. Walter Slenderman. Has anyone played with the themes from Leviathan? Monstrous inheritance, stagnation, being hunted, wondering if the world would be better without you? A lot of people's reaction to the game is &quot;people don't need lessons from monsters&quot;, and I think a lot of Beasts would believe that too. How do they cope with it? What new paths and callings do they find? <br /> <br /> I'm hoping this gets some coverage in the Player's Guide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T22:22:18-07:00","id":969667,"title":"","content":"&quot;Teaching lessons&quot; is just a justification for Beasts to feel better about their Feeding. It's just easier to do bad things to people if you feel justified in that they deserve having those bad things happen to them. That they deserve to &quot;learn a lesson.&quot; I can see some Beasts doing that to feel better about themselves, but I don't think all Beasts would particularly care or see themselves as having a responsibility. There has to be other philosophies out there.<br /> <br /> So I would say to think about what kind of justifications Beasts might conceive of as to why they should feel better of themselves for Feeding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T22:45:12-07:00","id":969677,"title":"","content":"It's a shame to me that the Homecoming is now a suggestion rather than the default, because there's a deep horror in &quot;you're not human and never have been,&quot; and that theme is only barely touched on in Beast and slightly in Werewolf. That's one thing I feel like Leviathan absolutely nailed, but between that and how I liked Heroes better when Beasts created them (and thus they basically were Ahabs) this thread risks derailing into &quot;I wish Beast was Leviathan.&quot;<br /> <br /> The theme I want to fixate on in the historical setting I'm planning is the idea of monstrosity as divinity, and how comfortable Beasts should be with their distance from mortal humanity. Stressing that Kinship is an uncomfortable thing and how it might be unpleasant to realize you have more in common with vampires and faeries than you do with your family and loved ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T22:46:56-07:00","id":969679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/969649-alternate-themes-and-motivations?p=969667#post969667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Teaching lessons&quot; is just a justification for Beasts to feel better about their Feeding.</div> </div> </div> </div>In about the same sense that &quot;drink responsibly&quot; is just a justification for alcoholics to feel better about their drinking.<br /> <br /> It's hard to be a person when you just follow your Hunger; most philosophies are going to necessarily involve adding some wrinkle to the animalistic straight line between eating and sleeping, whether it's expanding the borders of the Primordial Dream or influencing mortal society or playing matchmaker with inter-splat politics. Legend-as-introspection is an easy praxis for most Beasts to come to, provided they know what the Lair is and how it relates to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T22:49:31-07:00","id":969680,"title":"","content":"This isn't really a debate on the &quot;lessons&quot; idea. That's been argued to death. I think really going into &quot;family&quot; as a theme would be interesting. Do Beasts ever start families? Is Beasthood in any way hereditary? That was a great thing about Leviathan, something none of the other splats really had. <br /> <br /> The &quot;caught between two worlds&quot; thing could be lifted and changed from Werewolf, where you have the Beast trapped between the daylight world of their old life and the night world of monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T23:07:03-07:00","id":969687,"title":"","content":"For consideration, a collation:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">&quot;The inferiority you feel is actually the quality of a king. [You] know how small you are. And yet you still struggle to reach heights greater than you can imagine.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;A king without greed is even worse than a figurehead! [Who] can truly admire the martyr's thorny path? Who dreams of such an ending?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The king must be greedier than any other. He must laugh louder and rage harder. He must exemplify the extreme of all things, good and evil. That is why his retainers envy and adore him. And why the flames of aspiration, to be as the king is, can burn within his people. &quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;A king must live a life more vivid than any other and be a figure for all to admire! The king is the one who collects the envy of all his heroes and stands as their guide! Therefore, the king is not alone! For his will equals that of all his followers combined!&quot;</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T23:24:58-07:00","id":969695,"title":"","content":"Where is that from? It's very interesting. <br /> <br /> I kind of wish Beast had a splat or plot element based on organizations or ideologies of Beasts. Like, what happens when a bunch of Beasts get together and talk theology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T23:41:41-07:00","id":969702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/969649-alternate-themes-and-motivations?p=969687#post969687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For consideration, a collation:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">&amp;quot;The inferiority you feel is actually the quality of a king. [You] know how small you are. And yet you still struggle to reach heights greater than you can imagine.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;A king without greed is even worse than a figurehead! [Who] can truly admire the martyr's thorny path? Who dreams of such an ending?&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;The king must be greedier than any other. He must laugh louder and rage harder. He must exemplify the extreme of all things, good and evil. That is why his retainers envy and adore him. And why the flames of aspiration, to be as the king is, can burn within his people. &amp;quot;<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;A king must live a life more vivid than any other and be a figure for all to admire! The king is the one who collects the envy of all his heroes and stands as their guide! Therefore, the king is not alone! For his will equals that of all his followers combined!&amp;quot;</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, Iskander from Fate/Zero. I have to say, I love that character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T01:41:00-07:00","id":969762,"title":"","content":"Beast might be a good splat for &quot;rehab&quot; as a theme. Their Hunger is basically an addiction, and they're supposed to explore all the weird corners of the WoD, so going looking for some way to get food without hurting people could make a good game. (Admittedly you'd have to stop the answer just being Family Dinner). It's got an inbuilt philosophical conflict with Beasts who're feeding the normal way so that's a plus.<br /> <br /> You could also just invert lesson culture. Beasts are &quot;primordial&quot;, so by that definition the modern world has learnt a lot they could benefit from knowing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T04:01:59-07:00","id":969807,"title":"","content":"Most of the ways Beasts feed are essentially normal activities. The first version of the text - less so the one we eventually got, but it can still work that way - struck me as oddly suited, given their outre nature, to having protagonists live relatively normal lives and engage with the world much the way mortals do. So that would be one of my alternatives. They still consider their human life to be their real one, and continue to live it as much as they can. It doesn't stop them digging into the supernatural around them, but mostly for the purposes of protecting their lives, loved ones, and neighbourhoods (and feeding opportunities). The theme would be an exploration of the currents of power, abuse, and evil that we treat as socially normal and kind of don't notice.<br /> <br /> Another would be mediators between supernatural factions - take the family thing to its full extent. Their job is to gather the various supernatural factions into one community for the good of all.<br /> <br /> Another I had, I called the Raveners, who took their Hunger as &quot;categorical imperative&quot; to the full. Feeding their Horrors is <i>right</i>, and they do it without shame or guilt - not necessarily without restraint or conscience, as it needn't the <i>only</i> thing they take as right (being a monster means you get to choose how you act, not that you have to act monstrously at all times). Since we've had a thread about mortal cultists of the Dark Mother, I would probably add an element of encouraging humans to follow a similar course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T05:54:21-07:00","id":969838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/969649-alternate-themes-and-motivations?p=969702#post969702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, Iskander from Fate/Zero. I have to say, I love that character.</div> </div> </div> </div>is there anyone who doesn't love Rider?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T06:09:21-07:00","id":969843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/969649-alternate-themes-and-motivations?p=969838#post969838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is there anyone who doesn't love Rider?</div> </div> </div> </div>If there are, I've not met them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T11:49:12-07:00","id":970077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/969649-alternate-themes-and-motivations?p=969680#post969680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't really a debate on the &quot;lessons&quot; idea. That's been argued to death. I think really going into &quot;family&quot; as a theme would be interesting. Do Beasts ever start families? Is Beasthood in any way hereditary? That was a great thing about Leviathan, something none of the other splats really had.<br /> <br /> The &quot;caught between two worlds&quot; thing could be lifted and changed from Werewolf, where you have the Beast trapped between the daylight world of their old life and the night world of monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 13 actually has the answer to your hereditary question. Beasts aren't genetic and there's nothing stopping a Beast from settling down and having kids. I loved that letter in the old draft where the Beast apparently crippled a hero and left and then left the question of whether or not the kids will be more likely to take after the mom (the Beast) or the dad (the Hero). Never looked into Leviathan so not sure what specifics you're referring to there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T12:48:57-07:00","id":970848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/969649-alternate-themes-and-motivations#post969649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was wondering, what are some themes/motivations/justifications you've come up with and used, other than the &quot;teaching lessons&quot; theme? Because I think it can be done well, but I understand that a lot of people don't like it, and there's a lot more potential than just being J. Walter Slenderman. Has anyone played with the themes from Leviathan? Monstrous inheritance, stagnation, being hunted, wondering if the world would be better without you? A lot of people's reaction to the game is &quot;people don't need lessons from monsters&quot;, and I think a lot of Beasts would believe that too. How do they cope with it? What new paths and callings do they find?<br /> <br /> I'm hoping this gets some coverage in the Player's Guide.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly,I don't use the lesson thing. I just can't. Rationalization of abuse, as in &quot;I hurt them for their own good&quot;, resonates with bad experiences and affects me deeply. I get that most people probably don't share those experiences, but I don't get how including that notion could have looked like a good idea. And with the introduction of the concept of &quot;shock&quot;, it's clearly abuse we're talking about.<br /> Dealing with themes of abuse is complex and difficult, but I think trying to spin it as something positive can't be the right way to treat that subject.<br /> <br /> So, personally, I prefer to go with the version where Beasts could be interpreted as feeding though their actions no matter how people feel about them, rather than as feeding on the suffering caused by their actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T17:06:14-07:00","id":970989,"title":"","content":"It's not so much &quot;I hurt them for their own good&quot; as &quot;I have to hurt somebody so I don't starve, and I want to at least do it in a way that potentially enables growth so that it's not just meaningless, random violence&quot;<br /> <br /> That said, there are other, likely more palatable ways to direct Hungers to positive ends. For example: &quot;I have to put the fear of me into somebody, might as well be the otherwordly slavers from the Hedge&quot;<br /> <br /> You can be the Beast that becomes the hero (lower case intentional) After all, who knows better what monsters really lurk in the shadows, and which ones are truly antagonistic to humanity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T17:32:35-07:00","id":971012,"title":"","content":"Since I chimed in on quotes, a few quotes quotes in relation to the topic.<br /> <br /> &quot;Ye should understand too, really. Ah just need be ae bayonet. Ae bayonet named <i><b>divine punishment</b></i>. Ah wish ah'd been born ae storm. Or ae menace. Or ae single explosive. Nae heart, nae tears, just as ae terrible gale'd been good. If with a pierce of this ah can become <i>that</i>, then <i>sae</i> be it. Amen.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Dinnae cry, devil. Did nae ye become ae devil because ye did nae want tae cry? Man cries, his tears dry up, and run oot. Sae he becomes ae devil, reduced tae ae monster. He changes and perishes. Sae smile.&quot;<br /> <br /> Or, if you want the Shakespearean variant, &quot;Why dost thou laugh? it fits not with this hour.&quot;&quot;Why, I have not another tear to shed-&quot;<br /> <br /> And above all, deeper and most powerful:<br /> <br /> &quot;The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-27-2016, 12:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T17:57:56-07:00","id":971032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/969649-alternate-themes-and-motivations?p=970989#post970989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not so much &quot;I hurt them for their own good&quot; as &quot;I have to hurt somebody so I don't starve, and I want to at least do it in a way that potentially enables growth so that it's not just meaningless, random violence&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That not any better, really. It's strange because it's not so much the 'inflicting trauma to feed' part that bothers me. I've played Vampire without trouble. It's a matter of survival, not random violence.<br /> If it was about mitigating the evil Beasts have to do, there could e some sort of aftercare system.<br /> But the lessons add a level of perversity, if you'll forgive me the term, that horrify me. It's one thing if a victim/survivor of abuse or misfortune find a way to get something positive from the aftermath of their ordeal. It's another entirely when the abuser takes it upon themselves to frame their abuse as something other than abuse, or to assume they are in a position to teach their victims. This doesn't show respect or concern, but rather presumption and contempt.<br /> Just try to imagine anyone in court trying to invoke 'giving a lesson' as mitigating circumstances for an agression.<br /> Obviously, I'm biased about this, but still it still feels like something that should be adressed at some point.<br /> <br /> Edit: In fact, if lessons could be dissociated from feeding, they wouldn't be so bad. Still condescending, but not... tainted. I could see a Beast teaching whatever in their human existence, and feeding as monsters independantly from the teaching they do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":1405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","user":"Anteros","date":". 09-16-2016, 09:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T20:14:58-07:00","id":971110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/969649-alternate-themes-and-motivations?p=971032#post971032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That not any better, really. It's strange because it's not so much the 'inflicting trauma to feed' part that bothers me. I've played Vampire without trouble. It's a matter of survival, not random violence.<br /> If it was about mitigating the evil Beasts have to do, there could e some sort of aftercare system.<br /> But the lessons add a level of perversity, if you'll forgive me the term, that horrify me. It's one thing if a victim/survivor of abuse or misfortune find a way to get something positive from the aftermath of their ordeal. It's another entirely when the abuser takes it upon themselves to frame their abuse as something other than abuse, or to assume they are in a position to teach their victims. This doesn't show respect or concern, but rather presumption and contempt.<br /> Just try to imagine anyone in court trying to invoke 'giving a lesson' as mitigating circumstances for an agression.<br /> Obviously, I'm biased about this, but still it still feels like something that should be adressed at some point.<br /> <br /> Edit: In fact, if lessons could be dissociated from feeding, they wouldn't be so bad. Still condescending, but not... tainted. I could see a Beast teaching whatever in their human existence, and feeding as monsters independantly from the teaching they do.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why I think it was a mistake to have such a strong tie to Teaching Lessons with Beasts. I think Teaching Lessons would be fine as a philosophy that SOME Beasts have... But the book presents it too strong as being all present with Beasts and I think that was a wrong way to go about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T20:40:31-07:00","id":971117,"title":"","content":"<i>hey guys remember when gecko said this thread was not for debating the matter of lessons<br /> <br /> what ever happened to that</i><br /> <br /> <br /> The nature of the Beast lends itself well to exploration in general, between the myriad Environmental Immunities, the metaphysical placement at the borders of human experience, and the overall connection of the species to the bigger picture. The Begotten are cloaked in fear and driven by desire; few splats are better suited to the task of mapping the cosmos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T20:53:09-07:00","id":971122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/969649-alternate-themes-and-motivations?p=971117#post971117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>hey guys remember when gecko said this thread was not for debating the matter of lessons<br /> <br /> what ever happened to that</i></div> </div> </div> </div>You remember that elephant you weren't supposed to think about?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T21:22:59-07:00","id":971138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/969649-alternate-themes-and-motivations?p=971117#post971117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>hey guys remember when gecko said this thread was not for debating the matter of lessons<br /> <br /> what ever happened to that</i><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>My bad. Sorry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T09:47:25-07:00","id":976577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/969649-alternate-themes-and-motivations?p=971012#post971012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Ye should understand too, really. Ah just need be ae bayonet. Ae bayonet named <i><b>divine punishment</b></i>. Ah wish ah'd been born ae storm. Or ae menace. Or ae single explosive. Nae heart, nae tears, just as ae terrible gale'd been good. If with a pierce of this ah can become <i>that</i>, then <i>sae</i> be it. Amen.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Dinnae cry, devil. Did nae ye become ae devil because ye did nae want tae cry? Man cries, his tears dry up, and run oot. Sae he becomes ae devil, reduced tae ae monster. He changes and preishes. Sae smile.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Paladin Alexander Anderson?<br /> <br /> One theme I'd like to play with is &quot;Identity&quot; you are a Monster. But is that all you are? Is that all you can ever be? And what of others? I might see them as they really are.. conflicted and tortured monsters too most but to me? do i act with the crowd and treat them as they are.. or do i try to understand them more? Everyone needs someone to talk with to help... can I be that to everyone else? Should I be when I can barely understand who I Really am? I Am a Monster... but is that because of what I look like or because Humanity as a group doesn't like being placed into a food-chain that has them within it.. and not on top of it? Is it not the actions of someone that makes them a Monster?<br /> <br /> I Know it's sorta baked into the material.. but I think I think it could really be used for some good fodder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T21:42:18-07:00","id":976947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/969649-alternate-themes-and-motivations?p=976577#post976577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Paladin Alexander Anderson?</div> </div> </div> </div>For a Hero, he really gets some of the reasons why Beasts find comfort in their monstrosity.<br /> <br /> Being human is <i>hard</i>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T11:01:18-07:00","id":977845,"title":"","content":"For me a major theme is to come to terms with the fact that one has to harm others in a very direct way to survive. Beasts were functionally human before their homecoming so there will be some dissonance between their prior moral and ethics an the urges of their horrors. Some beast might try to find ways of feeding their hunger that are as painless as possible. A tyrant might become an athlete feeding on his victories over his opponents and awe of his fans, feeding his hunger in a socially accepted way. Others might try to focus the harm on people which deserve it according to their prior morals. A ravager might focus on sources of pollution justifying the destruction he causes by saying that he is improving the environment. Again others might try to balance the harm they do by helping many other people. A beast with the dragonfire atavism will be fireproof so why not become a firefighter and save people? Sure you will still have to rob some people to increase your hoard and will hurt them but you are also saving lives, so you can still contribute to society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10574-matthiasthalmann","name":"MatthiasThalmann","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T17:36:18-07:00","id":978065,"title":"","content":"I don't concern myself with reasons and motivations. The Beast is doing what it needs to survive.<br /> <br /> I don't see the rest of the family making excuses. Why should the Begotten feel any differently?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And besides, I think the very idea of relying on reasons and motivations makes you infinitely worse than somebody who has no choice in the matter. Beasts psychologically torment people and draw nourishment from their fear. When you start coming up with ways to justify that kind of behavior, it makes something far, far more dangerous!<br /> <br /> History has enough monsters who felt like they weren't accountable for their actions...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-28-2016, 08:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T01:34:54-07:00","id":978267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/969649-alternate-themes-and-motivations?p=978065#post978065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't concern myself with reasons and motivations. The Beast is doing what it needs to survive.<br /> <br /> I don't see the rest of the family making excuses. Why should the Begotten feel any differently?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And besides, I think the very idea of relying on reasons and motivations makes you infinitely worse than somebody who has no choice in the matter. Beasts psychologically torment people and draw nourishment from their fear. When you start coming up with ways to justify that kind of behavior, it makes something far, far more dangerous!<br /> <br /> History has enough monsters who felt like they weren't accountable for their actions...</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the reason I preferred the idea of Homecoming to Devouring, Then the Begotten are blameless for their condition. The Devouring specifically makes it a active choice of the to-be Beast, they choose to be a Monster... they make the reasoning that it's so they can teach people more if they have a better connection to the Dream (Since it seems like they did that before some of the time).<br /> <br /> The Homecoming is more a case of them suddenly realising that the monster that haunts them in their Dreams is just another part of them, a part that is Monsterous and Primal, it needs to Feed. It Must. It has needs, that it has to fulfill. And then accepting that part of themselves... letting it become the larger presence of the themselves. That to me makes it abit better... I'm thinking of using Homecoming as the more common thing.. and the Devouring the less common thing for if they find someone that wants to become a beast... Maybe as a way to reform a Hero or something (If that Hero was particularly monsterous before that... they might make them into a Beast to &quot;Help&quot; them)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T04:59:42-07:00","id":978312,"title":"","content":"I didn't know what the big difference between Homecoming and Devouring was, but based on your description, I assume it's similar to <i>adoption</i> into the family?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T05:12:03-07:00","id":978317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/969649-alternate-themes-and-motivations?p=978312#post978312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't know what the big difference between Homecoming and Devouring was, but based on your description, I assume it's similar to <i>adoption</i> into the family?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Homecoming is basically where you find out that <i>You were the monster all along </i>whereas the devouring is more like <i>You always had the potential to be a monster and you just needed a Beast to help you actually get there</i>. So kinda, I guess.<br /> <br /> I personally prefer the Homecoming route, but that's just me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T06:19:41-07:00","id":978337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/969649-alternate-themes-and-motivations?p=978317#post978317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Homecoming is basically where you find out that <i>You were the monster all along </i>whereas the devouring is more like <i>You always had the potential to be a monster and you just needed a Beast to help you actually get there</i>. So kinda, I guess.<br /> <br /> I personally prefer the Homecoming route, but that's just me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well, I won't turn down the idea of the Homecoming route. But I've always loved the idea of transmigration, that is, the ability to change from one state of existence to another. Werewolves, Vampires, Zombies, pretty much any monster than can turn you into one of them is fascinating to me.<br /> <br /> So personally, I'd include both origins in my story. There are natural born monsters, and there are people who became one later in life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-29-2016, 09:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T19:45:39-07:00","id":978795,"title":"","content":"&quot;Doing what I need to survive&quot; is in itself a justification. Recognizing that you have the ability to consciously decide how to sate your Hunger, and accepting a responsibility to do so in the least harmful way available is not the same as deciding you are right and everyone else is wrong. A Beast can absolutely attempt to be a net benefit to the society they operate in (supernatural, mortal, or both) and still be painfully aware that they may not be living up to that goal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T19:28:54-07:00","id":979428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/969649-alternate-themes-and-motivations?p=978795#post978795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Doing what I need to survive&quot; is in itself a justification. Recognizing that you have the ability to consciously decide how to sate your Hunger, and accepting a responsibility to do so in the least harmful way available is not the same as deciding you are right and everyone else is wrong. A Beast can absolutely attempt to be a net benefit to the society they operate in (supernatural, mortal, or both) and still be painfully aware that they may not be living up to that goal.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, no, I'm not saying the monster has to drain their victims dry in order to survive. In fact, a lot of them seem keen on <i>not doing</i> that as it causes too many problems in the long run.<br /> <br /> But if you start looking at feeding as anything other than <b>feeding</b>, then it sets you on a dangerous slope from which few ever climb back out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T20:25:02-07:00","id":979452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/969649-alternate-themes-and-motivations?p=979428#post979428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if you start looking at feeding as anything other than <b>feeding</b>, then it sets you on a dangerous slope from which few ever climb back out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where you're getting things backwards is that the problem that finding a purpose seeks to address is falling into the trap of feeding <i>for the sake of feeding</i>.<br /> <br /> &quot;Eat to live, don't live to eat&quot; goes down a lot smoother when you can properly dress and garnish the meal and share it with friends instead of frantically cramming last week's cold leftovers down your gullet because you need to fill your belly <i>right now</i> with <i>something</i>.<br /> <br /> And providing some form of compensation for your personal contribution to entropy generally helps keep you in a human mindset. An adult pays for their food, says grace, uses the proper fork, and all that civilized stuff; just sitting down in front of a meal and eating is for Children.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T20:50:49-07:00","id":979460,"title":"","content":"But you can &quot;eat to live&quot; without focusing on the aspect of being a monster. There are other things you can do with your life to make the world a better place.<br /> <br /> Any creature suffers when faced with malnutrition, but the Begotten are even worse. Refusing to feed causes their souls to run wild throughout the Dream and ultimately hurt more people than is necessary to survive. They already have a reason to keep themselves fed (public safety), they don't need to go looking for more.<br /> <br /> <br /> Like I said previously, history already has enough monsters who thought they weren't accountable for their actions. As long as somebody with power convinces themselves it's for a good cause, they are capable of doing some pretty terrible acts. Vigilante justice incites chaos and strife, the key to remaining civilized is realizing you're not exempt from the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-30-2016, 11:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T21:36:25-07:00","id":979488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/969649-alternate-themes-and-motivations?p=979460#post979460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you can &quot;eat to live&quot; without focusing on the aspect of being a monster. There are other things you can do with your life to make the world a better place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and one of the ways you do that is by <i>giving your choice of meal more thought than &quot;none at all&quot; or &quot;people I don't like.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Entropy is arbitrary enough without a personlike actor rubber-stamping any dark urge or bit of bad luck that crosses their metaphorical desk. You devise philosophies and guidelines and schools of thought to exert control over the otherwise-random blowback of extracting shouts from the great echo chamber of human society. Building secondary motivations reminds Beasts that they don't exist in a vacuum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}